WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.253
The children had a delightful lunch with Mademoiselle.

2
00:00:05.254 --> 00:00:10.212
She served them cakes and tarts, and made wreaths for their heads.

3
00:00:10.213 --> 00:00:14.292
She drew pictures and told stories about her own school days.

4
00:00:14.293 --> 00:00:20.523
"Draw us a picture of a theater," said Gerald.

5
00:00:20.524 --> 00:00:23.580
"Do you like plays?" asked Mabel.

6
00:00:23.581 --> 00:00:26.259
"Oh yes, I love them!"

7
00:00:26.260 --> 00:00:29.449
Mademoiselle concentrated on her drawing.

8
00:00:29.450 --> 00:00:33.166
The children looked at each other and smiled.

9
00:00:33.167 --> 00:00:36.961
"We'll put on a play for you tonight," said Jimmy.

10
00:00:36.962 --> 00:00:42.009
"And please, may Eliza come too?" asked Kathleen.

11
00:00:42.010 --> 00:00:47.817
"Of course," said Mademoiselle with a smile.

12
00:00:47.818 --> 00:00:51.289
Mademoiselle stayed in the sitting room as usual.

13
00:00:51.290 --> 00:00:54.685
It was a good thing that she was not trying to concentrate!

14
00:00:54.686 --> 00:01:00.432
The children came in and out all afternoon, asking for things.

15
00:01:00.433 --> 00:01:04.610
May they have the sofa cushions?

16
00:01:04.611 --> 00:01:06.982
May they have the clothesline?

17
00:01:06.983 --> 00:01:10.340
Did she have any brightly colored scarves they could borrow?

18
00:01:10.341 --> 00:01:17.372
May they have tea in the garden because the stage was in the dining room? At

19
00:01:17.373 --> 00:01:21.920
last Eliza rang the dinner bell. That

20
00:01:21.921 --> 00:01:26.870
was the signal for Mademoiselle to go into the dining room for the play. Several

21
00:01:26.871 --> 00:01:30.585
tables had been pushed together to make a stage. Rows

22
00:01:30.586 --> 00:01:35.836
of chairs were set out for an audience. Mademoiselle

23
00:01:35.837 --> 00:01:43.246
was surprised to see seven people sitting in these chairs. "Children,"

24
00:01:43.247 --> 00:01:47.608
she whispered through the stage curtains. "You

25
00:01:47.609 --> 00:01:51.332
should have asked me before you invited guests." The

26
00:01:51.333 --> 00:01:53.359
children laughed. "Turn

27
00:01:53.360 --> 00:01:59.027
up the lights," said Mabel. Mademoiselle

28
00:01:59.028 --> 00:02:02.437
looked again at the people in the audience. "Oh!

29
00:02:02.438 --> 00:02:08.234
They're not alive!" she cried in surprise. And

30
00:02:08.235 --> 00:02:10.900
indeed they were not. Their

31
00:02:10.901 --> 00:02:14.602
bodies were made of pillows and rolled-up blankets. Their

32
00:02:14.603 --> 00:02:17.486
spines were broom handles. Their

33
00:02:17.487 --> 00:02:21.987
arms and legs were hockey sticks and umbrellas. They

34
00:02:21.988 --> 00:02:27.222
were dressed in whatever coats, hats, and gloves the children could find. And

35
00:02:27.223 --> 00:02:31.406
their faces were paper masks made by Gerald. "You've

36
00:02:31.407 --> 00:02:36.691
made yourself an audience! Bravo!" said Mademoiselle. And

37
00:02:36.692 --> 00:02:40.158
she and Eliza clapped. They

38
00:02:40.159 --> 00:02:42.960
sat down and the curtain opened. "

39
00:02:42.961 --> 00:02:48.939
Beauty and the Beast ," announced a voice from

40
00:02:48.940 --> 00:02:53.758
backstage. The children had spent much time making their costumes and

41
00:02:53.759 --> 00:02:56.572
audience. So they'd had little time to

42
00:02:56.573 --> 00:03:00.098
rehearse. But they had fun acting out the fairy

43
00:03:00.099 --> 00:03:04.020
tale. As Beauty, Mabel wore her princess

44
00:03:04.021 --> 00:03:07.866
clothes. As the Beast, Gerald wore some small

45
00:03:07.867 --> 00:03:11.465
rugs. Jimmy and Kathleen played all the minor

46
00:03:11.466 --> 00:03:15.540
parts. At the end of the second scene, everyone was

47
00:03:15.541 --> 00:03:19.605
backstage. "You should give me the ring," Mabel said to

48
00:03:19.606 --> 00:03:22.314
Gerald. He'd forgotten that it was in his

49
00:03:22.315 --> 00:03:27.221
pocket. "I'll do it in the next

50
00:03:27.222 --> 00:03:31.368
scene." And he did, making the ring part of the

51
00:03:31.369 --> 00:03:34.782
play. He told Beauty that the ring was a magic

52
00:03:34.783 --> 00:03:37.476
ring. It would give her anything she

53
00:03:37.477 --> 00:03:43.128
wished. So to see him again, she simply had to put it on and make her wish.

54
00:03:43.129 --> 00:03:46.503
At last they came to the final scene.

55
00:03:46.504 --> 00:03:51.161
Beauty was reunited with Beast, who was really a prince.

56
00:03:51.162 --> 00:03:54.700
Mademoiselle and Eliza clapped and cheered.

57
00:03:54.701 --> 00:03:57.953
Mabel looked at the fake audience members.

58
00:03:57.954 --> 00:04:00.599
"I wish those creatures we made were alive.

59
00:04:00.600 --> 00:04:03.496
We'd get some real applause then."

60
00:04:03.497 --> 00:04:06.898
"I'm glad they aren't alive," said Gerald.

61
00:04:06.899 --> 00:04:09.347
"I feel silly when I look at them."

62
00:04:09.348 --> 00:04:12.218
And suddenly it happened.

63
00:04:12.219 --> 00:04:14.908
There was the sound of more clapping.

64
00:04:14.909 --> 00:04:19.002
Seven paper faces were looking eagerly up at the stage.

65
00:04:19.003 --> 00:04:21.794
The creatures had come alive!

66
00:04:21.795 --> 00:04:28.320
Mademoiselle and Eliza screamed and ran from the room.

67
00:04:28.321 --> 00:04:31.784
"Give me the ring!" Gerald said to Mabel.

68
00:04:31.785 --> 00:04:34.461
He put the ring on his finger and cried,

69
00:04:34.462 --> 00:04:37.869
"I wish those Ugly-Wuglies weren't alive!"

70
00:04:37.870 --> 00:04:42.095
But nothing changed.

71
00:04:42.096 --> 00:04:47.488
Mabel and Gerald followed the creatures out into the hallway.

72
00:04:47.489 --> 00:04:58.112
"Excuse me," one said to Gerald, "can you recommend a good hotel?"

